  "task_html": "<div class='task-block task-blue'><div class='task-block-label'>Info: Funktion → Wertetabelle</div><p style='font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 8px 0;'>Wenn du eine Funktion als Formel kennst, kannst du für jeden <strong>x</strong>-Wert den <strong>Funktionswert f(x)</strong> berechnen – einfach einsetzen und ausrechnen.</p><div style='background:#eff6ff;border-radius:8px;padding:8px 12px;font-size:13px;'>Beispiel: &nbsp;f(x) = 2x &nbsp;|&nbsp; f(3) = 2·3 = <strong>6</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; f(&minus;2) = 2·(&minus;2) = <strong>&minus;4</strong></div></div><p style='font-size:14px;margin:14px 0 6px 0;'><strong>a)</strong> Fülle die Wertetabelle für <strong>f(x) = 3x + 2</strong> aus.</p><div class='tbl-wrap'><table><thead><tr><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>x</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>&minus;2</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>&minus;1</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>0</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>1</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>2</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>3</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='row-label'>f(x)</td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='-4' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='-1' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='2' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='5' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='8' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='11' placeholder='?'></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style='background:#fffbeb;border:1.5px solid #fde68a;border-radius:8px;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;font-size:13px;'><strong>Hinweis: x²</strong> bedeutet x &middot; x (x mal sich selbst). &nbsp;Beispiel: (&minus;2)² = (&minus;2) &middot; (&minus;2) = <strong>4</strong> &nbsp;— Minus mal Minus = Plus!</div><p style='font-size:14px;margin:12px 0 6px 0;'><strong>b)</strong> Fülle die Wertetabelle für <strong>g(x) = x² &minus; 1</strong> aus.</p><div class='tbl-wrap'><table><thead><tr><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>x</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>&minus;2</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>&minus;1</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>0</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>1</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>2</th><th style='background:#d95f2b;'>3</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='row-label'>g(x)</td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='3' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='0' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='-1' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='0' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='3' placeholder='?'></td><td><input class='cell-input' data-ans='8' placeholder='?'></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class='check-bar'><button class='btn-check' onclick='checkStation(10)'>&#x2713; Überprüfen</button><button class='btn-reset' onclick='resetStation(10)'>&#x21BA; Zurücksetzen</button><span class='check-result' id='check-result-10'></span></div>",
  "sol_html": "<p style='font-size:14px;margin:0 0 8px 0;'><strong>a) f(x) = 3x + 2:</strong></p><div style='font-size:13px;line-height:2;margin-bottom:12px;'>f(&minus;2) = 3·(&minus;2)+2 = <strong>&minus;4</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; f(&minus;1) = <strong>&minus;1</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; f(0) = <strong>2</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; f(1) = <strong>5</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; f(2) = <strong>8</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; f(3) = <strong>11</strong></div><p style='font-size:14px;margin:0 0 8px 0;'><strong>b) g(x) = x² &minus; 1:</strong></p><div style='font-size:13px;line-height:2;'>g(&minus;2) = (&minus;2)²&minus;1 = 4&minus;1 = <strong>3</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; g(&minus;1) = <strong>0</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; g(0) = <strong>&minus;1</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; g(1) = <strong>0</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; g(2) = <strong>3</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; g(3) = <strong>8</strong></div><p style='font-size:12px;color:#555;margin-top:10px;'>Fällt dir was auf? Bei g gilt g(&minus;2)=g(2)=3 und g(&minus;1)=g(1)=0 – der Graph von g ist symmetrisch zur y-Achse.</p>"
}
